      "slug": "teta-and-jiddo",
      "featured": true,
      "level": { "en": "Family", "ar": "عيلة" },
      "title": {
        "en": "Talking to Teta & Jiddo",
        "ar": "الحكي مع تيتا وجدو"
      },
      "description": {
        "en": "The phrases that make grandparents light up on the phone.",
        "ar": "الجمل يلي بتضوّي وج تيتا وجدو عالتلفون."
      },
      "tip": {
        "en": "Half of Lebanese affection is blessings, not compliments. Allah ykhallik and Allah ya3tik el 3afye do more work than \"thank you\" ever will — use them constantly.",
        "ar": "نص الحنان اللبناني دعوات مش مجاملات. \"الله يخليك\" و\"الله يعطيك العافية\" بيعملوا أكتر من \"شكراً\" بكتير."
      },
      "challenge": {
        "en": "Call a Lebanese relative or friend and keep the first two minutes entirely in Lebanese — greeting, how are you, I missed you, say hi to everyone.",
        "ar": "اتصل بقريب أو صاحب لبناني وخلّي أول دقيقتين كلهن بالعربي."
      },
      "homework": {
        "en": "Write five sentences about your own family using teta, jiddo, 7abibe, and one blessing. Bring them to the next lesson.",
        "ar": "اكتب ٥ جمل عن عيلتك مستعمل تيتا، جدو، حبيبي، ودعوة وحدة."
      },
      "dialogue": [
